return array (
  'content' => '<p>PVD-coated metal furniture — coffee tables, consoles, custom benches — brings the same champagne and black language as partitions and doors into the furnished layer. In homes and apartments with staff cleaning, children and occasional monsoon humidity through open windows, care and finish choice matter as much as the design sketch.</p><h2>What PVD furniture includes</h2><p>Table bases, frame legs, metal aprons and decorative inserts in stainless with PVD finish. Tops may be stone, glass or wood — metal carries the durable decorative surface.</p><p>Explore <a href="/shop/bespoke-metal-furniture">bespoke metal furniture</a> and <a href="/shop/coffee-tables">coffee tables</a> for starting points.</p><h2>Finish selection for furniture</h2><p>Hairline champagne hides fine scratches better than mirror gold. Matte black suits high-touch family rooms. Rose gold fits boutique bedrooms with lower abrasion.</p><p>Compare tones in <a href="/blog/pvd-finish-selection-guide-gold-rose-gold-champagne-black">PVD finish guide</a> under your actual downlights.</p><h2>Daily care in homes and apartments</h2><p>Dust with soft dry cloth; damp microfibre for fingerprints. Avoid steel wool, scouring powder and chloride bleach cleaners common in some housekeeping cupboards.</p><p>Coasters on metal-framed stone tops prevent ring marks on stone, not PVD — but acidic drinks on unsealed stone need usual stone care.</p><h2>Humidity and placement</h2><p>Interior air-conditioned spaces suit 304 stainless PVD furniture standard. Avoid placing metal furniture in direct monsoon splash zones on open terraces without exterior-grade review.</p><p>Keep metal legs away from floor mopping pools — standing water affects stone tops and can wick into joint details over time.</p><h2>Customization workflow</h2><p>Share room dimensions, sofa height and preferred top material. Vyomika Atelier develops custom sizes from our Delhi studio with pan-India freight — programme depends on stone sourcing and finish batch — share scope for project-specific timing.</p><p>Coordinate with <a href="/studio/pvd-partitions">partition finishes</a> on open-plan living for one metal palette.</p><h2>Repair and refresh</h2><p>Deep scratches in PVD may need factory refinishing of component — not field spray paint. Document finish code on delivery for future matching.</p><h2>Housekeeping protocols for staff</h2><p>Brief housekeeping to avoid abrasive powders and steel scrubbers — same guidance as PVD doors and partitions. Soft microfibre with pH-neutral cleaner is sufficient for fingerprints.</p><p>Do not place hot pans directly on metal frames even when tops are stone — heat can affect adhesive joints on some composite tops over time.</p><h2>Top material interactions</h2><p>Marble tops need usual stone sealing; metal base care is independent. Glass tops show base detail — keep undersides dust-free for display effect.</p><p>Wood tops expand seasonally — confirm expansion gap detail where wood meets metal frame to avoid push-out in humid months.</p><h2>Custom sizing workflow</h2><p>Share sofa depth, seat height and rug boundary so console and coffee table dimensions feel intentional. CAD sketch with overall width and height prevents scale surprises in room.</p><p>Coordinate finish sample with <a href="/studio/pvd-partitions">partition PVD</a> and <a href="/shop/door-handles">door handles</a> before welding begins — late finish changes are costly.</p><h2>Long-term refresh options</h2><p>Individual components may be refinished or replaced if deeply scratched — document finish code on handover sheet. Field spray paint is not a durable match for vacuum-deposited PVD.</p><p>International enquiries are reviewed project by project — freight and crating for furniture sized pieces confirmed per order.</p><h2>Seasonal humidity in Indian homes</h2><p>Monsoon months increase ambient humidity even in air-conditioned homes when windows open for ventilation. Metal frames are unaffected; joint details between metal and wood tops deserve inspection once yearly for any movement or adhesive line opening.</p><h2>Display and art placement</h2><p>Console tables behind sofas often carry art and table lamps. Specify felt pads under objects and avoid dragging heavy frames across PVD surfaces. Scratches on hairline finishes are less visible than on mirror gold but still worth preventing during redecoration.</p><h3>Outdoor-adjacent furniture</h3><p>Semi-open verandas and balcony-adjacent living areas expose furniture to dust and occasional splash. Interior-grade PVD furniture is not typically specified for fully open terrace use — discuss scope if placement is borderline outdoor.</p><h2>Custom profiles beyond catalogue</h2><p>Trapezoidal bases, angled legs and integrated cable routes for AV consoles are feasible when dimensions and finish are locked before structural welding. Share reference sketches and top material weight so leg sizing is adequate.</p><h2>Handover documentation worth keeping</h2><p>Store finish sample code, cleaning instructions and fabricator contact on the owner handover sheet. Future reorder of matching legs or handles depends on batch reference — generic colour names are not enough for PVD matching years later.</p><p>When furniture sits in the same room as <a href="/blog/choosing-metal-coffee-table-luxury-interior">coffee tables</a> and partitions, photograph approved samples in situ at handover for warranty and insurance records.</p><h2>Insurance and move-day handling</h2><p>Wrap PVD corners during home moves — contact with other furniture edges causes scratches unrelated to manufacturing. Lift tables by base frames, not glass tops, when repositioning rooms.</p><p>For open-plan homes, align furniture metal with <a href="/studio/pvd-partitions">partition finishes</a> so one approved sample batch covers visible metal in the main living zone.</p><h2>Children and high-traffic zones</h2><p>Rounded table corners, stable bases and secure top fixing reduce tipping risk in family rooms. Anchor tall shelving units independently — furniture that leans against PVD partition panels should not transfer load to glass fixings.</p><p>Label furniture crates by room on delivery so installers place heavy stone-topped pieces correctly the first time — repositioning across finished floors risks scratches to both stone and PVD.</p><h2>Reorder and spare parts</h2><p>Keep one spare handle or pull on large projects where downtime matters — matching batch codes years later requires original order records. International enquiries are reviewed project by project for replacement hardware.</p><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>PVD furniture stays beautiful with gentle cleaning, sensible placement and finish chosen for touch level in each room. Customize dimensions and tops to the interior, but keep finish samples aligned with architectural metal elsewhere for a coherent Vyomika Atelier home.</p><p>See <a href="/shop/bespoke-metal-furniture">bespoke metal furniture</a>.</p><p>Browse <a href="/shop/coffee-tables">coffee tables</a>.</p><p>Read <a href="/blog/pvd-coating-explained">PVD coating explained</a>.</p><p>For a project-specific quotation, share floor plans or photos through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. Architects and interior designers may also begin from the <a href="/professionals">professionals collaboration page</a>.</p>',
